<BlogPost 
  title="Privacy Policy" 
  description="Privacy policy and GDPR compliance details."
  pubDate={new Date('2026-07-31')}
>
  <p>We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting any personal information processed through this website. This policy details how data is handled in compliance with applicable EU regulations (GDPR).</p>

  <h2>Data Collection & Analytics</h2>
  <p>We do not collect personal identifying information (such as your name, address, or phone number) unless you explicitly contact us. Like most websites, we may use basic web analytics and server logs to collect standard anonymous statistical data.</p>

  <h2>Cookies & Third-Party Vendors</h2>
  <p>This site uses basic cookies to enhance user experience and facilitate affiliate link attribution.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Amazon & Retail Partners:</strong> When you click on an affiliate link, a third-party cookie is stored on your browser to attribute potential purchases. Amazon's tracking and cookie processing are governed by Amazon's Privacy Notice.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Anonymous usage metrics may be collected to help us understand which guides are most helpful.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your GDPR Rights</h2>
  <p>If you reside in the European Union, you have specific rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The right to request access to any personal data we may hold about you.</li>
    <li>The right to request correction or deletion of your personal data.</li>
    <li>The right to object to or restrict processing of your data.</li>
  </ul>
</BlogPost>
